    topic: "Learning to ride a bicycle to work",
    passage: "Until last spring, Otabek Mirzayev drove to work every day. His office was only seven kilometres from his apartment, but the journey took forty minutes in heavy traffic and cost him a fortune in petrol. He also spent most of the day sitting, first in his car and then at his desk, and he had started to feel stiff and tired. When his company announced a scheme which offered employees a cheap loan to buy a bicycle, he decided to try it, although he had not ridden a bike since he was a teenager.\n\nHe bought a simple grey bicycle with a basket and a good lock. His wife, Zilola, who often cycled with their children on Sundays, gave him a few lessons in a quiet park to help him regain his balance. At first he wobbled dangerously and, in the second lesson, fell into a bush while the children laughed. After a week, however, he felt confident enough to try the route to work early on a Saturday morning when the streets were empty.\n\nThe first official working day on the bike was a revelation. The journey took only twenty-five minutes because he could use a path along a canal and avoid the congested main road. He arrived with a slight headache from the unfamiliar effort but also with a clear mind. Over the following weeks, he learned several practical lessons. He bought a helmet and a bright jacket, after a taxi nearly hit him. He kept a spare shirt in the office because he sweated in warm weather. And he checked the weather forecast every evening, since rain made the paths dangerously slippery.\n\nThe results after six months were impressive. Otabek had lost five kilograms, his blood pressure was lower, and he had saved enough money on fuel to pay for the bicycle twice. Two colleagues, inspired by his example, also started cycling, and now the three of them ride together every Wednesday.\n\nOtabek admits that cycling is not perfect in every situation. In January, when the temperature fell to minus eight, he returned to the car for two weeks. Nevertheless, he is convinced that he will never go back to driving every day.",
